# Where the contact form posts. In production this is the site's own function,
# which sends the email itself — see netlify/functions/enquiry.js and the
# "Contact form" section of the README.
VITE_CONTACT_FORM_ENDPOINT=/api/enquiry

# --- server side, Netlify environment variables only ---------------------
# These are NOT VITE_ prefixed and must never be: Vite inlines VITE_* into the
# public bundle, which would publish the API key. They are read by the function
# at request time and set in Netlify's UI — or, for `netlify dev`, in .env.local,
# which is gitignored.
#
# RESEND_API_KEY=  the transactional mail API key (starts re_)
# MAIL_FROM=       enquiries@send.njhsportstherapy.co.uk — send-only, no mailbox
# MAIL_FROM_NAME=  NJH Website
# MAIL_TO=         defaults to njhpilates@gmail.com
# MAIL_BCC=        optional archive copy
#
# Before the domain is verified in Resend, an account is held in a sandbox that
# only accepts MAIL_FROM=onboarding@resend.dev and only delivers to the address
# the Resend account was opened with. The live account was opened with
# njhpilates@gmail.com precisely so that restriction lands on the address the
# form should reach anyway — so MAIL_TO is already final and only MAIL_FROM
# changes when the domain is verified. No code changes between them.
